WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.989
Inside the PostgreSQL

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.333
19 release notes

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.801
The new REPACK

00:00:04.613 --> 00:00:06.039
command reclaims disk

00:00:05.851 --> 00:00:07.443
space and reorganizes

00:00:07.254 --> 00:00:07.973
tables

00:00:08.009 --> 00:00:09.141
and its concurrent

00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:10.084
mode doesn't block

00:00:09.896 --> 00:00:11.169
reads or writes

00:00:11.686 --> 00:00:13.136
Logical replication

00:00:12.948 --> 00:00:13.690
can now be

00:00:13.502 --> 00:00:14.516
turned on without

00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:15.129
a restart

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.827
sequence values replicate

00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:17.204
too

00:00:17.311 --> 00:00:18.053
and a new

00:00:17.865 --> 00:00:19.244
WAIT command enables

00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:20.211
read-your-writes on

00:00:20.023 --> 00:00:20.931
standbys

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:22.248
Heads up

00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:23.262
max locks per

00:00:23.074 --> 00:00:24.547
transaction now defaults

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:26.293
to 128 instead

00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:27.118
of 64

00:00:27.248 --> 00:00:27.932
and a new

00:00:27.744 --> 00:00:29.807
64-bit unsigned oid8

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:30.786
data type arrives

00:00:30.904 --> 00:00:32.153
plus more jsonpath

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:32.967
string methods

00:00:33.486 --> 00:00:34.500
Full story on

00:00:34.311 --> 00:00:35.207
the dashboard
